---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import skills from '../data/skills.json';
import experience from '../data/experience.json';
---

<Base nav="about" title="About" description="About Aman Pathak: PhD scholar in hardware security and computer architecture at BITS Pilani Goa.">
  <PageHead title="About" kanji="人" sub="PhD scholar · hardware security · RISC-V · low-level software" />

  <p>
    I'm a PhD scholar in the Department of Computer Science and Information Systems at
    BITS Pilani, KK Birla Goa Campus, working at the intersection of hardware security,
    RISC-V architectures, and low-level software. My current work spans microarchitectural
    side-channel attacks and their mitigation, memory encryption, formal verification of
    cache coherency, and the security of CXL memory fabrics. I have six patents filed in
    the RISC-V space covering data-flow integrity, crypto engines, and on-chip ML, and
    earlier I designed Ku/X-band antennas at KIIT.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside of research I spend a lot of time building things close to the metal: a TCP/IP
    stack from scratch, a malloc replacement, a cycle-accurate 6502 emulator, a container
    runtime using raw namespaces and seccomp, a bytecode VM in Go, and neural networks
    built purely from matrix operations. This is not an exhaustive list; I keep adding
    projects to my <a href={site.github}>GitHub profile</a> as a hobby. I also write about
    these topics on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>, and I teach sometimes.
  </p>
  <p class="meta">
    A C program is nothing but bytes in memory; there is no abstraction beyond that you
    have to take on faith. More than low levels <i>per se</i>, I am interested in the
    stripped-down, non-abstracted, naked-truth stuff.
  </p>

  <h2 data-kanji="歴">Experience</h2>
  {experience.map((e) => (
    <>
      <h3>{e.role} <small>({e.date})</small></h3>
      <p class="meta" style="margin-top:-0.3rem">{e.org}</p>
      <ul>
        {e.bullets.map((b) => <li>{b}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </>
  ))}

  <h2 data-kanji="技">Skills</h2>
  <dl class="rows">
    {skills.map((group) => (
      <div>
        <dt>{group.label}</dt>
        <dd>{group.items.join(', ')}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 data-kanji="信">Contact</h2>
  <dl class="rows">
    <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd></div>
    <div><dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href={site.github}>github.com/vajradevam</a></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Web</dt><dd><a href="/">vajradevam.in</a></dd></div>
    <div><dt>RSS</dt><dd><a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
</Base>
